WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.420
We have to admit there's something insidious and detestable

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.100
about late night television, a kind of vicious circle.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.960
It's hard to realize until you actually go to a taping

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.080
and the warm-up comedian gauges your laugh on a 1 to 10 volume scale,

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.360
and instructs you that you're only in about a 7

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.700
and you need to keep it up and turn it up for every little joke you're about to see

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.080
because the microphones are way up in the ceiling and they won't hear you otherwise.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.320
It begins to dawn on you after about 10 cheerless guffaws

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.740
that you came to the taping because you thought the show was funny,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.880
and you thought the show was funny because all the jokes were followed by laughs and cheers,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.360
and the laughs and cheers were forced to make

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.800
are what's causing the audience at home to think the show is funny,

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:47.320
and it's why they want to come to the taping themselves, which they do and they laugh,

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.220
and this cycle begins again.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.660
Disappointing as this is,

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.320
it's also truly absurd.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.360
A self-generating absurdity that appears normal to us because it's all we know.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.700
And if a really smart and innovative comedian

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.320
wanted to draw attention to the normalization of this absurd American ritual,

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:12.320
perhaps the first thing to do would be to grab hold of the absurdity dial and turn it way up.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.960
"You get it? All right, let's just- oh"

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.380
"That's the biggest joint I've ever seen at Hogwarts.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.780
"I don't think this is the right eh- edition. "

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.360
"We're gonna keep going with this and we're gonna see

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.960
"when we hit the pixelation. How are we doing here? "

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.900
"This is a very strange show. "

